<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3770] GridLogThrottle.warn ignores the exception</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3770</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There are two ways to fix this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Make sure that &lt;tt&gt;warn()&lt;/tt&gt; method prints out the stack trace of the provided exception.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Remove exception parameter from the &lt;tt&gt;warn()&lt;/tt&gt; method and replace all such usages with &lt;tt&gt;error()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;I personally think that the second approach is clearer.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
