                            <comment id="15508682" author="roman_s" created="Wed, 21 Sep 2016 04:21:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vkulichenko&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vkulichenko&quot;&gt;vkulichenko&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Considering &lt;tt&gt;U.warn&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;U.quietAndWarn&lt;/tt&gt; does not handle exceptions (but &lt;tt&gt;U.error&lt;/tt&gt; does), I suppose the 2nd approach is what we need.&lt;br/&gt;
Do you think we can change method signatures here because these methods are in the internal package, or should we create new while leaving old but making them deprecated?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15508786" author="vkulichenko" created="Wed, 21 Sep 2016 05:14:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Roman,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let&apos;s just change signatures and refactor the code. This is not part of public API, so no reason to preserve compatibility.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
